---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
---

<Content
  title="WP Flame Community vs Pro — A Packaging Hypothesis"
  description="Review the proposed Community and Pro boundary, the principles that keep free diagnosis useful, and what remains unvalidated before launch."
  eyebrow="Community vs Pro"
  heading="Community for one-off diagnosis. Pro for continuous confidence."
  intro="That is the leading packaging hypothesis—not a launched edition contract. Paid design-partner evidence will decide the final boundary, pricing, licensing, and support model."
>
  <section class="content-section content-section--narrow" aria-labelledby="hypothesis-title">
    <div class="content-status-panel">
      <span class="content-status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div>
        <strong id="hypothesis-title">No public Pro plan is available yet</strong>
        <p>
          The current paid design-partner programme uses founder-led onboarding and manual commercial
          validation. It is not the final Community or Pro offer, and no monthly or annual public
          pricing should be treated as settled until real paid tests are reviewed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <div class="content-section-header">
      <p class="content-eyebrow">Packaging principles</p>
      <h2 id="principles-title">Monetize recurring workflow, not measurement truth.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="content-grid content-grid--3">
      <article class="content-card"><h3>Community solves a complete problem</h3><p>A user should be able to reproduce one incident, find a credible supported contributor, and share redacted evidence without an expiry or deliberately unusable result.</p></article>
      <article class="content-card"><h3>Accuracy is identical</h3><p>Community and Pro must share the same trace schema, attribution truth, scoring rules, capability model, and essential findings.</p></article>
      <article class="content-card"><h3>Pro earns renewal</h3><p>Recurring value should come from monitoring, longer history, compatible comparisons, reports, support, and professional multi-workflow operation.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
    <div class="content-section-header">
      <p class="content-eyebrow">Leading edition hypothesis</p>
      <h2 id="boundary-title">A useful free diagnosis; paid ongoing confidence.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="content-table-wrap">
      <table class="content-table">
        <caption>Provisional Community and Pro boundary for validation</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Workflow</th><th scope="col">Community candidate</th><th scope="col">Pro candidate</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Capture</th><td>Manual page/workflow capture; Safe, Standard, and focused one-shot Deep where supported.</td><td>Controlled automatic sampling and saved monitored workflows.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Evidence</th><td>Interactive trace, capability report, span detail, and basic top measured opportunities.</td><td>Same measurement truth with recurring aggregation and workflow-specific context.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">History</th><td>Bounded recent local history sufficient for one-off diagnosis.</td><td>Longer configurable history with route distributions and cohort controls.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Comparison</th><td>Single-trace evidence and a redacted export.</td><td>Compatible before/after cohorts, saved comparisons, and professional reports.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Support</th><td>Documentation and a public support channel.</td><td>Ticket support; priority routing only after measured support capacity exists.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Sites</th><td>No account required for the local Community workflow.</td><td>Active production-site licensing hypothesis; staging/local should not consume activations.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="shared-truth-title">
    <div class="content-grid content-grid--2">
      <article class="content-card content-card--accent">
        <p class="content-kicker">Always shared</p>
        <h2 id="shared-truth-title">Measurement truth</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Supported spans mean the same thing in both editions.</li>
          <li>Unavailable capability remains unknown, not a better score.</li>
          <li>Essential diagnosis is not withheld from a Community trace.</li>
          <li>Redaction, storage health, and retention controls are not premium safety features.</li>
          <li>Licensing failure must not silently change local trace accuracy.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="content-card content-card--purple">
        <p class="content-kicker">Validate before building</p>
        <h2>Open commercial questions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Which recurring workflows cause professionals to pay and renew?</li>
          <li>Do reports materially affect agency conversion or retention?</li>
          <li>Which site-count ladder fits actual portfolios?</li>
          <li>What support response is sustainable?</li>
          <li>Should connected fleet services exist at all before multi-site demand is proven?</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--narrow" aria-labelledby="expiry-title">
    <div class="content-callout">
      <h2 id="expiry-title">Provisional license-expiry principle</h2>
      <p>
        Expiration should leave already-installed local monitoring functionality running. Updates,
        support, and separately delivered connected services may stop. The final behavior must be
        documented and tested before public checkout.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--narrow" aria-labelledby="next-title">
    <div class="content-section-header"><p class="content-eyebrow">What happens now</p><h2 id="next-title">Design partners validate the boundary with real work.</h2></div>
    <p>
      The programme asks agencies and operators to bring a real slow dynamic workflow, complete a
      controlled diagnosis, and show which parts of monitoring, comparison, reporting, and support
      they actually use. The resulting paid behavior—not survey enthusiasm—will set the public offer.
    </p>
    <div class="content-link-list">
      <a href="/design-partner/">Review the paid programme</a>
      <a href="/product/">Read the product contract</a>
      <a href="/terms/">Read current programme terms</a>
      <a href="/privacy/">Read data handling</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Content>
